[ASSIST] Here's a simple end user API for 3D camera animation in TypeScript:

```typescript
export interface Camera {
  id: number;
  name: string;
  position: { x: number; y: number; z: number };
  rotation: { x: number; y: number; z: number };
  animation: {
    name: string;
    duration: number;
    frames: [{ position: { x: number; y: number; z: number }; rotation: { x: number; y: number; z: number } }];
  };
}

export interface Animation {
  id: number;
  name: string;
  duration: number;
  frames: [{ position: { x: number; y: number; z: number }; rotation: { x: number; y: number; z: number } }];
}

export interface CameraService {
  getCameras(): Promise<Camera[]>;
  getCamera(id: number): Promise<Camera>;
  createCamera(name: string, position: { x: number; y: number; z: number }, rotation: { x: number; y: number; z: number }): Promise<Camera>;
  updateCamera(id: number, name: string, position: { x: number; y: number; z: number }, rotation: { x: number; y: number; z: number }): Promise<Camera>;
  deleteCamera(id: number): Promise<void>;

  getAnimations(): Promise<Animation[]>;
  getAnimation(id: number): Promise<Animation>;
  createAnimation(name: string, duration: number, frames: [{ position: { x: number; y: number; z: number }; rotation: { x: number; y: number; z: number } }]): Promise<Animation>;
  updateAnimation(id: number, name: string, duration: number, frames: [{ position: { x: number; y: number; z: number }; rotation: { x: number; y: number; z: number } }]): Promise<Animation>;
  deleteAnimation(id: number): Promise<void>;
}

export interface CameraController {
  getCameras(): void;
  getCamera(id: number): void;
  createCamera(name: string, position: { x: number; y: number; z: number }, rotation: { x: number; y: number; z: number }): void;
  updateCamera(id: number, name: string, position: { x: number; y: number; z: number }, rotation: { x: number; y: number; z: number }): void;
  deleteCamera(id: number): void;

  getAnimations(): void;
  getAnimation(id: number): void;
  createAnimation(name: string, duration: number, frames: [{ position: { x: number; y: number; z: number }; rotation: { x: number; y: number; z: number } }]): void;
  updateAnimation(id: number, name: string, duration: number, frames: [{ position: { x: number; y: number; z: number }; rotation: { x: number; y: number; z: number } }]): void;
  deleteAnimation(id: number): void;
}
```

This API provides methods for getting, creating, updating, and deleting cameras and animations. Each camera and animation has a unique ID, name, position, rotation, and animation. The animation consists of a name, duration, and an array of frames, each containing a position and rotation.

The `CameraService` interface defines the methods for interacting with the camera and animation data, while the `CameraController` interface defines the methods for presenting the data to the end user.

You can use this API to create a web application for 3D camera animation, where users can create, edit, and delete cameras and animations, and view the animations in a 3D environment.

Response B: 

[ASSIST] Here's a basic structure for your end user API for 3D camera animation in TypeScript:

```typescript
import { Camera, Scene } from 'three';

class AnimationAPI {
  private scene: Scene;
  private camera: Camera;

  constructor(scene: Scene, camera: Camera) {
    this.scene = scene;
    this.camera = camera;
  }

  public animate(duration: number, easing: string = 'linear') {
    const animation = new Animation(this.camera, duration, easing);
    animation.start();
  }

  public pauseAnimation() {
    const animation = this.camera.animation;
    if (animation) {
      animation.pause();
    }
  }

  public resumeAnimation() {
    const animation = this.camera.animation;
    if (animation) {
      animation.resume();
    }
  }

  public stopAnimation() {
    const animation = this.camera.animation;
    if (animation) {
      animation.stop();
    }
  }
}

class Animation {
  private camera: Camera;
  private duration: number;
  private easing: string;
  private animation: AnimationClip;

  constructor(camera: Camera, duration: number, easing: string) {
    this.camera = camera;
    this.duration = duration;
    this.easing = easing;
    this.animation = new AnimationClip(duration, this.easing);
  }

  public start() {
    this.camera.animation = this.animation;
    this.animation.play();
  }

  public pause() {
    this.camera.animation = null;
    this.animation.pause();
  }

  public resume() {
    this.camera.animation = this.animation;
    this.animation.resume();
  }

  public stop() {
    this.camera.animation = null;
    this.animation.stop();
  }
}

// Example usage
const scene = new Scene();
const camera = new Camera();
const animationAPI = new AnimationAPI(scene, camera);

animationAPI.animate(2, 'easeOutQuad');
animationAPI.pauseAnimation();
animationAPI.resumeAnimation();
animationAPI.stopAnimation();
```

This API provides basic animation functionality for a 3D camera. You can customize the animation duration, easing, and other properties as needed.

